--   RPCs                            request_session_change, approve_session_change, reject_session_change,
--                                   withdraw_session_change, session_change_signatures (D4).
--   9 readers repointed             the 8 R7 readers refuse a cancelled session; my_department_rollup's next-event union
--                                   skips it. Each = the VERBATIM live body + one inserted block; the post-condition proves
--                                   md5(new body minus that block) = the live md5.
--   housekeeping (R8)               swap_week_dates + move_week dropped (both were anon/authenticated-executable; neither is
--                                   called anywhere; move_week writes a column that doesn't exist).
--
-- DECISIONS THE RECORD DID NOT SPELL OUT (flagged for the gate review — claude/B4C_TrainingOverhaul_Slice7_DB_Draft.md):
--   D1 "Upcoming" = the drill's date >= today in Central; same-day counts. A pending request whose drill date has passed, or
--      whose session has since been attended / finalized / changed state, is EXPIRED by the approve call (returned, not
--      raised — a raise would roll the expiry back). A new request on that session first expires stale pending ones.
--   D2 The requests table is readable by is_leadership() OR is_training_manager() (dept-scoped): a training officer who is a
--      plain Member is an approver but not "leadership" — under a leadership-only policy they couldn't see what they sign.
--   D3 A cancelled session is locked like a finalized one (its protected fields change only under the flag) — its record
--      can't be silently rewritten while cancelled; Restore unlocks it.
--   D4 session_change_signatures(request_id) is the on-demand signature read (column grants make it the only path for
--      authenticated). Same read gate as the table.
--   D5 Approving a cancel also closes any open QR sign-in on that session (signin_open=false, token cleared).
--   D6 The approver must be a training manager ≠ the initiator. "Never a Project Admin" holds through is_training_manager()
--      itself (its DA arm is the Department Admin ROLE); a PA who is ALSO a registered training officer is a TO and counts.
--   D7 current_signin_token returns NULL (no code) for a cancelled session rather than raising — the officer page polls it.
--   D8 Reject: any OTHER training manager, reason >= 10 chars. Withdraw: the initiator only.
--   D9 Signature = 'data:image/png;base64,' + base64, total length <= 204800 characters ("<= 200 KB").
